---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import Panel from "~/components/illustration-kit/Panel.astro"
import SvgFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/SvgFigure.astro"
---

<IllustrationFigure
  name="newcombs-paradox"
  lead="The money is already in place. Which boxes should you take?"
>
  <SvgFigure
    name="newcomb-boxes"
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-md"
    viewBox="0 0 360 186"
    title="An open box and a closed box"
    desc="Box A is open and always contains $1,000. Box B is closed and already contains either $1,000,000 or nothing, based on an earlier prediction of your choice."
  >
    <g fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">
      <text x="94" y="24">
        Box A · open
      </text>
      <text x="266" y="24">
        Box B · closed
      </text>
    </g>
    <g fill="none" stroke="var(--color-stroke)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
      <path d="M30 66 V144 H158 V66" />
      <path d="M30 66 L13 51 M158 66 L175 51" />
      <rect x="202" y="51" width="128" height="93" />
      <path d="M202 68 H330" />
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">
      <text x="94" y="114" font-size="23">
        $1,000
      </text>
      <text x="266" y="116" font-size="29">
        ?
      </text>
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14">
      <text x="94" y="171">
        Always there
      </text>
      <text x="266" y="171">
        $0 or $1 million
      </text>
    </g>
  </SvgFigure>

  <p>
    A near-perfect predictor put $1 million in B if it expected you to take B alone, and nothing
    if it expected you to take both. It made its prediction before you chose.
  </p>

  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <Panel accent="blue" title="Take both boxes">
      <p>Whatever is in B, taking A too gets you an extra $1,000.</p>
    </Panel>
    <Panel accent="green" title="Take only Box B">
      <p>
        The predictor is almost always right. People who take only B almost always find $1
        million inside.
      </p>
    </Panel>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    Taking both is better for either fixed content. Taking only B is usually linked to getting
    the million. Which argument should you follow?
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
